   {
    "id": "p1",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "content": [
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "World Radio Day falls on February 13 every year. Do you know "
     },
     {
      "t": "blank",
      "id": "b1",
      "number": 1
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": " created radio?"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p2",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "content": [
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "Guglielmo Marconi was an "
     },
     {
      "t": "blank",
      "id": "b2",
      "number": 2,
      "hint": {
       "baseWord": "Italy"
      }
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": " scientist. He was born in 1874. At the age of 21, he "
     },
     {
      "t": "blank",
      "id": "b3",
      "number": 3,
      "hint": {
       "baseWord": "build"
      }
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": " the world’s first "
     },
     {
      "t": "gloss",
      "v": "wireless telegraph",
      "zh": "无线电报机"
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": ". He succeeded in "
     },
     {
      "t": "blank",
      "id": "b4",
      "number": 4,
      "hint": {
       "baseWord": "send"
      }
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": " messages by radio waves instead of wires. This machine was the starting point of radio."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p3",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "content": [
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "How does radio work? Well, the sounds are turned into radio waves. These waves travel "
     },
     {
      "t": "blank",
      "id": "b5",
      "number": 5
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": " the air. And the radio receiver turns them back into the sounds we "
     },
     {
      "t": "blank",
      "id": "b6",
      "number": 6
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p4",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "content": [
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "In the early 1920s, radio became "
     },
     {
      "t": "blank",
      "id": "b7",
      "number": 7,
      "hint": {
       "baseWord": "wide"
      }
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": " used. There were more than 500 radio stations for news, sports, music shows and more. People spent hours listening to these shows every day. This was the "
     },
     {
      "t": "blank",
      "id": "b8",
      "number": 8,
      "hint": {
       "baseWord": "begin"
      }
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": " of the “Golden Age of Radio”."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p5",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "content": [
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "By now, radio has been around for "
     },
     {
      "t": "blank",
      "id": "b9",
      "number": 9,
      "hint": {
       "baseWord": "century"
      }
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": ". And it continues to grow. World Radio Day highlights the "
     },
     {
      "t": "blank",
      "id": "b10",
      "number": 10,
      "hint": {
       "baseWord": "important"
      }
     },
     {
      "t": "text",
      "v": " of this great invention. Tune in to your favourite radio station and enjoy!"
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
